<h2>Where a Public Adjuster Can Help, and the Limits</h2>
<p>A public adjuster can be useful on a flood loss, but it is important to be clear about what one can and cannot do.</p>
<h3>Where we can help</h3>
<ul>
<li>Reviewing your flood policy and any homeowners or commercial policy to identify which damage goes where.</li>
<li>Documenting the high-water line, removed drywall and flooring, and damaged equipment.</li>
<li>Preparing a line-item building estimate and a contents inventory.</li>
<li>Helping prepare the proof of loss within the policy deadline.</li>
<li>Pursuing a separate wind or hail claim if the same storm damaged the roof.</li>
</ul>
<h3>The limits</h3>
<ul>
<li>If you had no flood policy, a public adjuster cannot make a homeowners policy pay for rising water that the policy excludes.</li>
<li>We cannot change NFIP coverage limits or exclusions.</li>
<li>The NFIP does not pay public adjuster fees; any fee comes from your recovery under a written contract. Fees are disclosed in a written contract before any work begins; Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement.</li>
<li>Federal disaster assistance, when available after a declared disaster, is a separate program from insurance.</li>
<li>Public adjusters do not give legal advice. Questions about suing on a flood claim belong with a Texas attorney.</li>
</ul>

<h2>First Steps After a Flood</h2>
<ol>
<li>Stay out of floodwater and do not drive through low water crossings.</li>
<li>Photograph the water line on walls, fences, and contents before cleanup.</li>
<li>Report the loss to your flood insurer, and to your property insurer if the roof or walls were also damaged.</li>
<li>Start drying and remove wet materials to limit mold, keeping samples and photos.</li>
<li>List damaged contents with age, brand, and approximate cost.</li>
</ol>
<p>Our <a href="/claim-documentation-checklist/">claim documentation checklist</a> can help you stay organized. If you want a second set of eyes on your flood or storm claim, San Antonio Public Adjuster offers a <a href="/free-claim-review/">free claim review</a>.</p>
